{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA912642","title":"Re-utilization of Fenton sludge as an iron source for the promotion of anammox processes Meta","description":"In this study, GF and Fe/GF carriers were used in anammox systems to investigated the feasibility of re-utilization of Fenton sludge. After 90 days cultivation, the NRR of Fe/GF-CSTR reached 72.85%, while it was 52.68% in the GF-CSTR. The loaded iron in GF could promote the cell biosynthesis and metabolic ability of anammox bacteria. Furthermore, Fe/GF also caused the increase microbial diversity contributing to the functional genes related to nitrogen transformation, resulting in the increase on reactor performance. This study offers a novel approach of the re-utilization of Fenton sludge in anammox processes, showing the high potential of anammox engineering application.","center":"Nanjing Agricultural University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2022/12/15 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN32247903","sludge","uncertain",null,"2022-09-06",2022,"CN","Jiangsu",1799962,"Nanjing","probable",null,null,"China: Nanjing","reactor2 d90 sample",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN32247904","sludge","uncertain",null,"2022-09-06",2022,"CN","Jiangsu",1799962,"Nanjing","probable",null,null,"China: Nanjing","reactor1 d90 sample",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN32247905","sludge","uncertain",null,"2022-09-06",2022,"CN","Jiangsu",1799962,"Nanjing","probable",null,null,"China: Nanjing","reactor2 d40 sample",null,null,null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN32247906","sludge","uncertain",null,"2022-09-06",2022,"CN","Jiangsu",1799962,"Nanjing","proba